ation execution, live routing, current folder ownership, GCE Stack materialization, and stale live references**.\n\nHere’s the prompt I’d give Luce:\n\n:::writing{variant=\"document\" id=\"48321\" title=\"Luce Truth Pass — Pre-Drive Reconciliation\"}\nLUCE — TRUTH TELLER / GROUND-TRUTH PASS\n\nAUTHORITY: Don  \nMODE: READ-ONLY RECONNAISSANCE  \nPURPOSE: Verify the current local-machine truth required before Coda updates Google Drive or creates the next generation of GCE workstream/project anchors.\n\nDO NOT:\n- modify files\n- rename folders\n- move anything\n- edit AGENTS.md\n- change routing\n- change Command Center\n- change VoiceBridge\n- change project files\n- clean anything up\n- normalize historical names\n- infer completion because a migration plan exists\n\nYour job is to answer what the machine actually proves.\n\nCURRENT FROZEN DOCTRINE\n\nDon — final authority  \nCoda — governance / canon / reconciliation  \nVittorio — technical advisor / warboard / challenge  \nChiave — architecture  \nNico — implementation hammer / builder  \nCorrado — quant engine only  \nFalcon — data acquisition / retrieval  \nTalon — operations / routing / coordination  \nKeel — deployment / operational build support / stability  \nLuce — verification / ground truth  \nRagno — Principal Consultant / integration / translation when needed  \nMagpie — registry / secretary  \nPigeon — transport  \nRaven — documentation\n\nCore separation:\n\nVittorio advises.  \nChiave architects.  \nNico builds.  \nCorrado computes.\n\nMODEL != SEAT.\n\nHistorical Kimi, Calibro, old Corrado, and other legacy references must remain provenance where historically correct. We are only trying to determine whether any of those identities still control LIVE routing or current authority.\n\n==================================================\n1. FROZEN-SEAT MIGRATION — DID IT ACTUALLY HAPPEN?\n==================================================\n\nFind and inspect the migration planning artifacts if present, including:\n\n- 20260922-KEEL-GCE-FROZEN-SEAT-MIGRATION-PLAN.md\n- 20260922-KEEL-GCE-FROZEN-SEAT-MIGRATION-PHASE0-DELTAS.md\n\nThen independently inspect the machine.\n\nReturn:\n\nA. EXECUTED\nB. PARTIALLY EXECUTED\nC. PLANNED BUT NOT EXECUTED\nD. UNKNOWN\n\nDo not infer from the plan. Prove from current state.\n\nSpecifically verify whether:\n\n- Vittorio has a live canonical identity/bootstrap surface.\n- Nico has a live canonical identity/bootstrap surface.\n- Corrado currently resolves as quant-only.\n- Chiave remains architecture.\n- Kimi has been removed from the LIVE operating-seat namespace.\n- Calibro has been retired from LIVE current authority or is only present through an approved temporary Calibro → Nico compatibility alias.\n- There is NO Corrado → Vittorio alias.\n- There is NO Kimi → Vittorio alias.\n\nFor every conclusion give the exact path/file/evidence.\n\n==================================================\n2. LIVE ROUTER / BOOTSTRAP TRUTH\n==================================================\n\nInspect current live dispatch/bootstrap surfaces.\n\nAt minimum check:\n\n- profile-root AGENTS.md\n- GCE_SEAT_ROUTER.md\n- opencode.json\n- GCE_IDENTITY seat folders / AGENTS.md files\n- any other current router/bootstrap registry actually used\n\nDetermine:\n\n- Which seat names are currently dispatchable?\n- Which paths do they resolve to?\n- Are any retired names still canonical routing targets?\n- Are any aliases active?\n- Does a fresh command such as \"load <seat> bootstrap\" resolve to the intended current seat?\n- Are there any silent wrong-seat routes?\n\nDo not modify or test destructively.\n\nReturn a compact routing table:\n\nCOMMAND / NAME  \nCURRENT TARGET  \nPATH  \nSTATUS: CURRENT / ALIAS / HISTORICAL / STALE / BROKEN  \nFINDING\n\n==================================================\n3. NAME/PATH COUPLING BLAST-RADIUS RECHECK\n==================================================\n\nEarlier Luce work found seat-name/path coupling across several