 clean current state. fileciteturn49file0L3-L13\n\n## What actually survived\n\nThe build converged on a deliberately tiny capture primitive:\n\n**Action Button → Record Audio → Save File → playable local `.m4a`**\n\nThat path was successfully proven on the actual iPhone. The key doctrine is:\n\n> **Raw audio is the authoritative evidence. Transcription is a derived projection.**\n\nThe earlier Dictate Text → Scriptable → JSON path was superseded by a better primitive; it was **not** proven universally broken. fileciteturn49file0L21-L53\n\nThat distinction is excellent and should stay intact.\n\n## Current project truth\n\nThese are the project-canonical decisions:\n\n- audio-first capture;\n- `Record Audio → Save File`;\n- raw audio = source evidence;\n- transcription = derived/rebuildable;\n- Scriptable exits the capture critical path;\n- one immutable recording per thought;\n- flat folder + timestamp-derived filenames is the preferred next direction, but still provisional until tested. fileciteturn49file0L213-L283\n\nThe current implementation artifact is the **`Capture Thought`** iPhone Shortcut, with a successful `WalkingCapture.m4a` bench artifact. The old `GCE_Capture` Scriptable code survives only as build-history/supporting evidence. fileciteturn49file0L405-L463\n\n---\n\n# Reconciliation against Wave 1 / Wave 2\n\n### GCE Stack\n**MATCH.**\n\nThis is exactly the kind of thing the GCE Stack parent is supposed to own:\n\n- capture;\n- local device primitive;\n- later transport/sync;\n- VoiceBridge-adjacent integration eventually;\n- local-to-desktop pipeline later.\n\nSo this strengthens the case for the parent structure:\n\n**GCE Stack**  \n→ Walking Capture / Mobile Capture  \n→ Web Bridge / scraper  \n→ VoiceBridge  \n→ transport/sync  \n→ runtime plumbing / local services  \n→ adapters/utilities\n\nNo separate parent project needed.\n\n### Framework\n**No current Framework change.**\n\nThere are several potentially reusable lessons, especially:\n\n- evidence before interpretation;\n- preserve source vs derived projection;\n- distinguish **superseded** from **failed**;\n- prove the smallest native primitive before adding orchestration.\n\nBut the source itself correctly says these are **reconciliation candidates**, not automatic canon. fileciteturn49file0L475-L517\n\nThat is the right classification.\n\n---\n\n# What is dead and should stay dead\n\nDo **not** resurrect:\n\n- Dictate Text → Scriptable → JSON as the capture architecture;\n- dictated text as “raw” evidence;\n- Scriptable as required for safe capture;\n- sequential `capture_001` counters;\n- dynamic daily folders;\n- sidecar JSON in the capture transaction;\n- transcription in the critical path;\n- Siri invocation as the v0.1 trigger;\n- Tailscale, VoiceBridge, desktop, network, Drive, or AI dependencies in v0.1. fileciteturn49file0L638-L655\n\nThis is important because the whole success of this POC came from **shrinking the critical path**.\n\n---\n\n# Open work — still valid\n\nThe remaining work is implementation hardening, not architecture:\n\n1. unique timestamp/random-suffix filenames;\n2. fixed flat `WalkingCapture` folder;\n3. Action Button binding;\n4. locked-screen test;\n5. rapid-fire collision test;\n6. long-ramble test;\n7. 20-thought walking field test;\n8. transcription layer only **after** raw capture proves stable. fileciteturn49file0L548-L634\n\nThat means this is actually a very healthy project state:\n\n**No conceptual blocker. Only bench hardening and field validation remain.** fileciteturn49file0L661-L679\n\n---\n\n# Wave 3 registry entry\n\n**W3-01 — Walking Capture / Mobile Thought Capture**\n\n**Classification:** `GCE STACK SUBPROJECT — ACTIVE POC`  \n**Authority:** Don  \n**Current stage:** verified primitive → hardening / field test  \n**Current truth:** audio-first native iPhone capture  \n**Framework impact:** candidates only  \n**Drive state:** no governing artifact yet  \n**Next route:** dedicated **Walking Capture / GCE Stack implementation chat**  \n**Do not create separate parent project:** correct\n\n## One useful addition to our master action ledger\n\nWhen we materialize the GCE Stack parent, **Walking Capture should be explicitly listed as a subproject/component**, with the current boundary:\n\n> **Capture first. Interpretation and transport later.**\n\nThat will prevent future chats from re-attaching VoiceBridge, AI, transcription, or network plumbing to the critical capture path prematurely.\n\n**Wave 3 is now open, and W3-01 is cleanly registered.**", "text_chars": 4900, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "df8d6e6a-796b-4c58-97a0-7e41234f9e6a", "role": "tool", "role_name": "api_tool", "created_at": 1790202538.4434347, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["text", "text"], "text": "Make sure to include fileciteturn49file0L5-L8 in your response to cite this file, or to surface it as a link. Replace the placeholder line range with the actual line range from the result that best fits the snippet you want to surface with the citation. If you cite multiple files, use a separate complete `filecite` marker for each file. Never put multiple `turnNfileM` targets inside a single `filecite` marker.\nUse ref_id \"turn49file0\" to reference this file. For broad questions or unknown locations, retrieve relevant chunks with `files.search` scoped to this file. Use `files.find` only for exact text, and use `files.read` for a known range or to expand relevant results. Full file size: 700 file lines.\n[L1] # 1. SESSION HEADER\n\n[L3] **CHAT / WORKSTREAM:** GCE Peter Throwing Shit at the Wall — Walking Capture / iPhone Thought-Capture POC  \n[L4] **PRIMARY DOMAIN:** GCE Stack / Project  \n[L5] 