3] Transcription, JSON, daily summaries, AI classification, desktop transport, VoiceBridge, Tailscale, network synchronization, and downstream reconciliation remain outside the capture critical path.\n\n---\n\n[L57] # 3. ACCOMPLISHMENTS BY DATE\n\n[L59] ## DATE: 2026-09-22\n\n[L61] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \n[L62] Walking Capture v0.1 was scoped as a phone-only POC. Initial architecture used iPhone Shortcuts with Dictate Text feeding Scriptable, intended to create immutable JSON captures.\n\n[L64] **DECISION / RESULT:**  \n[L65] Phone-only scope was locked. Network, desktop, VoiceBridge, Tailscale, Drive, AI classification, and background processing were explicitly excluded from v0.1.\n\n[L67] **WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Don authority; Coda design/support.\n\n[L69] **STATUS:** accepted\n\n---\n\n[L73] ## DATE: 2026-09-22\n\n[L75] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \n[L76] A Scriptable capture implementation named `GCE_Capture` was developed to receive shortcut text and write immutable JSON under a WalkingCapture directory.\n\n[L78] **DECISION / RESULT:**  \n[L79] The implementation included UUID capture IDs, local timestamps, source/capture metadata, overwrite protection, and terminal statuses such as `ok`, `cancelled`, and `fail`.\n\n[L81] **WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Coda implementation support under Don direction.\n\n[L83] **STATUS:** implemented, later superseded from the capture critical path\n\n---\n\n[L87] ## DATE: 2026-09-22\n\n[L89] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \n[L90] Actual iPhone Shortcuts behavior was pressure-tested through screenshots and live interaction.\n\n[L92] **DECISION / RESULT:**  \n[L93] Several assumed Shortcuts / Scriptable input behaviors were disproven by the actual UI:\n[L94] - Scriptable’s visible `Parameter` field opened a file picker.\n[L95] - Scriptable’s `Texts` editor did not behave like a normal persistent literal-text field.\n[L96] - The intended Dictate Text → composed Text → Scriptable parameter path was not successfully proven