| Strategic Advisor / Governance / Canon / Reconciliation | Maintains Framework boundary, reconciles Stack lessons upward, prevents Stack from becoming Framework canon by accident |\n| **Vittorio** | Technical Advisor / Warboard / Challenge | Challenges technical direction, assumptions, readiness and tradeoffs; **does not become builder** |\n| **Chiave** | Architecture | Invoked when GCE Stack work materially requires architecture; owns architecture decisions, not routine implementation |\n| **Nico** | Implementation Hammer / Builder | Primary design-to-build and system-creation seat for accepted Stack work |\n| **Corrado** | Quant Engine | Normally **not part of GCE Stack lifecycle** unless the Stack task genuinely requires mathematical/quantitative execution |\n| **Falcon** | Data Acquisition / Retrieval | Data collection/retrieval where Stack components require external/current data |\n| **Talon** | Operations / Routing / Coordination | Routes work, coordinates execution, maintains operational flow |\n| **Keel** | Deployment / Operational Build Support / Stability | Deployment, operational cleanup, service stability, bounded implementation support |\n| **Luce** | Verification / Ground Truth | Independent truthing and post-change verification |\n| **Ragno** | Principal Consultant / Integration / Translation | Cross-system translation/integration when genuinely needed; not a mandatory gate |\n| **Magpie** | Registry / Secretary | Registry and administrative recordkeeping |\n| **Pigeon** | Transport | Transport-specific function when invoked |\n| **Raven** | Documentation / Durable Record | Durable documentation and record creation |\n\n### Frozen technical separation\n\n**Vittorio advises.**  \n**Chiave architects.**  \n**Nico builds.**  \n**Corrado computes.**\n\nThat separation applies inside GCE Stack just as it does elsewhere. memcite\n\n# GCE Stack's Actual Identity\n\nThe Stack is best understood as the **technical enabling layer**.\n\nIt owns things such as:\n\n**Capture → Transport → Synchronization → Runtime → Services → Adapters → Utilities → Operational tooling**\n\nIt does **not** own:\n\n- Framework governance;\n- seat authority;\n- Framework canon;\n- Edge Crew methodology;\n- Quant methodology;\n- business/project-specific decision authority;\n- model-selection authority merely because a model is used by a Stack component.\n\n## MODEL ≠ SEAT remains absolute\n\nFor example:\n\n- WebBridge may run using Kimi technology.\n- Ragno may currently have Kimi/Moonshot runtime occupancy.\n- Keel may execute through OpenCode / Big Pickle.\n- Nico may use whichever approved implementation runtime is appropriate.\n\nNone of those runtime choices change the identity, role, or authority of the seat.\n\n# Current Component Placement\n\n### **Walking Capture**\n**GCE Stack → Capture / Recovery → Mobile Capture**\n\nCurrent canonical primitive:\n\n`Action Button → Record Audio → Save File`\n\nAudio = authority/source evidence.  \nTranscription = downstream projection.\n\n### **WebBridge**\n**GCE Stack → Web Capture / Scraping**\n\nThe old “Kimi Web Bridge” name may remain valid implementation/history, but **Kimi does not define the parent-project identity**.\n\n### **VoiceBridge**\n**GCE Stack → Voice / Interaction technical component**\n\nTechnical implementation belongs under Stack. User workflow may cross other domains, but the plumbing belongs here.\n\n### **Command Center**\nFramework-facing operational UI/control surface, with the **technical implementation/support layer in GCE Stack**.\n\n### **Transport / State Sync**\nCross-component infrastructure. These should not become separate top-level projects merely because they have implementation depth.\n\n# Canonical project boundary\n\nThe model I would freeze is:\n\n```text\nGCE FRAMEWORK\nAuthority / Governance / Canon / Taxonomy\n        │\n        │ governs boundaries\n        ▼\nGCE STACK\nReusable technical substrate / tooling / services\n        │\n        │ supports\n        ▼\nGCE PROJECTS\nEdge Crew, future applications, project-specific systems\n```\n\nAnd the critical rule is:\n\n> **Using GCE Stack infrastructure does not transfer implementation authority from the consuming project to GCE Stack.**\n\nLikewise:\n\n> **A technical pattern discovered in GCE Stack does not become Framework doctrine until it is reconciled and explicitly adopted.**\n\nThat is the clean frozen canonical identity I would use for the **GCE Stack parent artifact and new GCE Stack chat bootstrap**.", "text_chars": 6093, "code_blocks": 2, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "9191f21e-dca3-403d-8bd1-007dda0eca7f", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790226745.310117, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_context", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "ce489356-a655-4238-9785-ced8fe3bd86d", "role": "system", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790226746.8678365, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 0, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 1, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "c84691af-8780-42a9-97f3-53336480ce65", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790226748.093134, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_ch